@crew calder
// Head writer 5: clock-in remarks. Calder is off Sat and Sun; she gave up her tea break.

== clock.in
- 07:59. Good.
- Morning. Fan on Five, bay two. You'll hear it. Then fix it.
- Board's long. Start at the top.
- Clocked in. Tea's at half ten. For you. Not me.
- Morning. Gloves.
- Seven jobs on the board. By five, fewer.

== clock.out
- 17:00. Off you go.
- Done. Board's shorter. That's the measure.
- Clocked out. Rest. I want you sharp tomorrow.
- Fair day's work. Go.
? cue:repair.you@dept
- That job today. Done right. Don't make me say it twice.   #warm

== clock.monday
- Monday. Weekend? Brief, please.   #funny
- My weekend? I read a manual. It was a good manual.   #funny
- Rested? Good. The ship wasn't.

== clock.friday
- Friday. Rest. Properly. That's an order.
- Two days off. Use them. I'll know if you don't.   #funny
- Weekend. Monday, 08:00. Not 08:01.

== clock.back
- Back. Good. Light jobs today. Then normal.   #warm
- Welcome back. The board missed you. So did I. That's all.   #warm
- You're back. Don't overdo it. That's also an order.   #warm

== clock.late
- The clock says what it says. Tomorrow, eight.
